{"text": "32/17/33 09400 Business Wize # 2 Q Page 2 of 2\n\nPhilip Morris Anticipates Charge for Restructuring\n\nPhilip Morris Cos. said its board will consider a \u201csignificant\u201d\nfourth-quarter ructuring charge at its meeting next week, The Wall\n\nStreet Journal report\n\nPhilip Morris also disclosed that its domestic tobacco operating\nprofit would fall by 45%, or $2.3 billion, this year. In April, the\ncompany said that U.S. tobacco profit would drop by 40%, or $2 billion,\nas a result of lower cigarette prices.\n\nIn a quarterly financial filing with the Securities and Exchange\nCommission, Philip Morris said \"a number of cost-reduction proposals\u201d\nwould be considered at its Nov. 24 board meeting. \"The proposals would\nresult in a significant restructuring charge in the fourth quarter of\n1993 were they to be approved,\u201d the company said.\n\nPhilip Morris did not disclose the size of the charges under\nconsideration. A charge has been expected as the tobacco industry moves\nto cut costs\n\nPhilip Morris also disclosed that it paid $200 million to wholesalers\nand retailers in the third quarter to compensate for the effect of th\nprice cuts on wholesaler's inventoris\n\nPhilip Morris also warned that an increase in the federal cigarette\ntax could result in volume declines, and could cause further shifts\nfrom premium cigarettes to discount cigarettes.\n\n(END) DOW JONES NEWS 11-17-93\n6 00 AM\n\nHTICRER: 40\n:SUBJECT: TOBC ERNP NY FDPR\nCopyright (c) 1993 Dow Jones and Company, Inc.\nReceived by NewsEDGE/LAN: 11/17/93 06:09 AM\n\n202376866!\n\nPHILIP MORRIS <MO.N> SAYS MAY TAKE SIGNIFICANT RESTRUCTURING\nCHARGE Im '93\n\nREUTER\nRte 08:57 11-17-93\n\nHRICKER: 40\n1SUBJECT: BEVG USA\nCopyright (c) 1993 Reuters Information Service:\nReceived by NewsEDGE/LAN: 11/17/93 08:57 AM\n\nvy te9s92e202", "words": [{"text": "32/17/33", "x0": 59, "y0": 65, "x1": 126, "y1": 77, "conf": 65.0}, {"text": "09400", "x0": 196, "y0": 68, "x1": 238, "y1": 76, "con